      "text": "Find \nrank\n(\n𝐴\n)\n given that \nNull\n(\n𝐴\n)\n=\n{\n[\n2\n𝑥\n1\n+\n3\n𝑥\n2\n−\n3\n𝑥\n3\n\n\n𝑥\n1\n+\n3\n𝑥\n2\n+\n3\n𝑥\n3\n\n\n−\n3\n𝑥\n3\n\n\n−\n3\n𝑥\n2\n+\n3\n𝑥\n3\n]\n|\n𝑥\n1\n,\n𝑥\n2\n,\n𝑥\n3\n∈\n𝑅\n}\n.\n\nChoose an answer\nIncorrect choice left unselected.\n\n0\n\nIncorrect choice left unselected.\n\n3\n\n✓\nCorrect choice selected.\n\n1\n\nIncorrect choice left unselected.\n\n4\n\nIncorrect choice left unselected.\n\n2\n\nCORRECT\nPreview only\nSolution:\n\nAnswer · correct value:\n\n1\n\nAccording to the rank-nullity theorem, if \n𝐴\n is a matrix with \n𝑛\n columns, then\n\nrank\n(\n𝐴\n)\n+\nnullity\n(\n𝐴\n)\n=\n𝑛\n.\n\nFor the given matrix, we have \n𝑛\n=\n4\n,\n since this is the number of components in each of the vectors of the null space.\n\nAlso, since\n\nNull\n(\n𝐴\n)\n=\n{\n𝑥\n1\n[\n2\n\n\n1\n\n\n0\n\n\n0\n]\n+\n𝑥\n2\n[\n3\n\n\n3\n\n\n0\n\n\n−\n3\n]\n+\n𝑥\n3\n[\n−\n3\n\n\n3\n\n\n−\n3\n\n\n3\n]\n|\n𝑥\n1\n,\n𝑥\n2\n,\n𝑥\n3\n∈\n𝑅\n}\n\nwe conclude that \nnullity\n(\n𝐴\n)\n=\n3.\n\nTherefore,\n\nrank\n(\n𝐴\n)\n+\nnullity\n(\n𝐴\n)\n\t\n=\n𝑛\n\n\nrank\n(\n𝐴\n)\n+\n3\n\t\n=\n4\n\n\nrank\n(\n𝐴\n)\n\t\n=\n4\n−\n3\n\n\t\n=\n1.\n\nBack to study →",
